{#- allowed_hosts is required by homepage itself (Next.js host header
   check) — every hostname/IP:port it'll be reached as must be listed or
   it 500s.

   puid/pgid: the uid:gid the container runs as (Podman `User=`), not
   PUID/PGID env: without PUID the image's entrypoint skips its chown and
   su-exec and needs no capabilities. Nothing on the host is owned by it —
   see tmpfs.

   tmpfs: /app/config is a tmpfs; Salt's settings.yaml/services.yaml are
   bound read-only into it (root-owned, 0644 on the host), the image copies
   its other skeleton files in on start. /app/.next/cache: Next.js' image
   cache. So the root fs stays read-only and the host keeps no state.

   podman: spec overrides for the container (keys: formulas/podman README). #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'image': 'ghcr.io/gethomepage/homepage',
    'tag': 'v2.8.0',
    'container_name': 'homepage',
    'host_port': 3000,
    'config_dir': '/opt/homepage/config',
    'puid': 1000,
    'pgid': 1000,
    'timezone': 'Etc/UTC',
    'allowed_hosts': 'localhost:3000,127.0.0.1:3000',
    'tmpfs': ['/app/config', '/app/.next/cache'],
    'podman': {},
} %}
{%- set homepage = salt['pillar.get']('homepage:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
